=== WEB SOURCE ANALYSIS ===
Data sources (web useQuery/useMutation, kept under the same query shape at the Swift call sites):
  useVehicles                      → GET  /vehicles
  useTeslaChargingSessions(vin?)   → GET  /tesla/charging/sessions{?vin}
  useRefreshTeslaChargingSessions  → POST /tesla/charging/sessions/refresh{?vin,date_from,date_to}
Wire types ported (SI on disk — energy in Wh; peak power is the wire kW value the web reads directly):
  TeslaFleetChargingSession (session_id, vin, site_location_name, charge_start_datetime,
    total_energy_added_wh, peak_power_kw, charge_duration_s, charger_type, currency_code, total_cost,
    per_kwh_rate, latitude, longitude, fetched_at), TeslaFleetChargingSummary, TeslaFleetChargingResponse.
Module-scope helpers ported: buildMonthlyCost (monthlyCost), the range filter (sessions memo),
  sortedSessions, formatDurationSeconds (duration), vehicleOptions, mapPoints, is403 (refreshForbidden),
  exportSelectedCsv (ChargingSessionsCSV).
SI converter ported (P1/S5): convertEnergyFromSI (Wh→kWh); converted only at the render boundary.
10 panels: business banner (GlassPanel1) · controls bar (GlassPanel2) · 5 summary StatCards
  (Total Sessions / Energy / Cost / Avg Cost-kWh / Peak Power) · Monthly-Charging-Cost ChartContainer ·
  Session-Locations map (GlassPanel9) · sessions table (GlassPanel10).
2 charts (Swift Charts / MapKit, never WKWebView): ChartContainer wrapper · BarChart (BarMark).
  The Session-Locations panel is a first-party MapKit `Map` (the manifest scores the dedicated
  TeslaChargingSessionsMap unit separately, Maps=0; this page's GlassPanel9 renders it natively).
4 data states: loading · empty · error · success.
32 i18n strings (see STRING COVERAGE).

